      "id": 5479,
      "name": "WriterRyan",
      "username": "WriterRyan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/writerryan/{size}/2710_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-01-30T15:48:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hey all. I’ve noticed that there are a lot of question threads floating around - some of which haven’t been answered and some of which haven’t been given an official rulings post. In order to sort some stuff out and make answers a bit easier to find, I’m starting a thread to get any/all questions you could possibly have. As I get questions, I’ll work on getting the answers for them and then make sure that they’re put into the rulings board.</p>\n<p>So, tl;dr, ask any rules questions you have starting…now!</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">THE QUESTIONS</span><br>\nIs playing the top card of a hero deck is the same as a hero playing a card (it has been stated that putting a card into play from the trash or the deck is not the same as playing a card)?<br>\n<font color=\"red\">Unanswered</font></p>\n<p>Does the source of the action of playing a card matter (such as when a card from an environment or villain deck says to “put the top card of the hero decks into play”)?<br>\n<font color=\"red\">Unanswered</font></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:09.105Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
